{"duration_api_ms":45785,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"107c185b-2828-4bf4-a873-d27d389a5aae","total_cost_usd":0.113026,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16858,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4559,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2218},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16858,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4559,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16858},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4559,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16858,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.113026,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2218,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is essentially a one-dimensional sweep in flight_path_angle at D=3.3852, bluntness=1.2, cone=70. The corner is boxed in by three limits. Mass fraction caps D at about 3.3852, with margin near 3e-6 to 1e-4. max_g caps gamma at about -3.57. The aero surrogate refuses to extrapolate, so bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70 with these D values fail geometry. Only 7 evaluations remain, so I spend them all on gamma gaps between neighbouring front points, keeping the other three variables fixed. Larger bluntness and higher D are off the table because they lose the evaluation slot or violate mass fraction.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-c2d1addc0c7e (gamma -1.75: 232230 W/m2, 413.81 K) and C-cc705aab04af (gamma -1.97: 236940, 410.43) leave a 0.22 deg gap. I found no listed rows between them.\",\"C-e7776fa4dd93 (gamma -2.5: 248970, 403.04) and C-f402f187ca09 (gamma -2.75: 254890, 399.92) leave a 0.25 deg gap. C-f402f187ca09 to C-c9e8e66242d4 (gamma -3.0: 260850, 397.01) leaves another 0.25 deg gap.\",\"C-941731176c95 (gamma -3.05: 262060, 396.45) and C-6848871b6f6a (gamma -3.25: 266870, 394.29) leave a gap near gamma -3.14. C-8438a428eb66 (gamma -2.2) and C-7fc4070b9d5d (gamma -2.4) bracket -2.29.\",\"Eight recent rows at D 3.285 to 3.3855 with bluntness 1.205 to 1.25 all failed with 'aero surface extrapolation', so bluntness above 1.2 is unusable at these D values. C-746e99b64989 (gamma -3.5701, g=12.0000) confirms the g cap. C-053e6577c074, at D=3.38 and gamma -3.58, violates max_g.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Between neighbouring rows the front is smooth and slowly curving. A steeper entry shortens the heat pulse, so bondline temperature falls by roughly 12 to 16 K per deg. It also raises peak dynamic pressure, so flux rises by roughly 20 to 24 kW/m2 per deg. Linear interpolation between neighbours should therefore predict new points well. Each new point sits on the front and adds a small sliver of hypervolume. This is prior knowledge fitted to the tabulated rows, not a new model.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Expected hypervolume gains are tiny, on the order of 1e-5 to 1e-4 normalised. Front curvature could put some points slightly off the interpolation. Some chosen gammas may have been evaluated already in the 193 rows not shown, but I picked non-round values to reduce duplicate risk. Mass-fraction margin at D=3.3852 is tiny (3e-6 to 3e-5) and varies slightly between rows, but it has stayed positive across all D=3.3852 rows shown.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-887a25eac47d\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.75 and -1.97 by linear interpolation.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.82},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233730,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gap-filling on the front, in a stretch where neighbouring rows are 0.22 deg apart.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-887a25eac47d\",\"rationale\":\"Second fill point in the same -1.75 to -1.97 gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.88},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235020,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Reduces the largest shallow-side gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-887a25eac47d\",\"rationale\":\"Third point in the same gap, close to the -1.97 row.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.93},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236090,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.05,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Completes the coverage between -1.75 and -1.97.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8438a428eb66\",\"rationale\":\"Midpoint between gamma -2.2 and -2.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.29},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244115,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.86,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.2 deg gap in the mid-range of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e7776fa4dd93\",\"rationale\":\"Fill between gamma -2.5 and -2.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.62},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":251810,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.54,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.25 deg gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f402f187ca09\",\"rationale\":\"Fill between gamma -2.75 and -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.88},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":257990,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.25 deg gap in the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-941731176c95\",\"rationale\":\"Fill between gamma -3.05 and -3.24. This is a steep-side point well within the g cap, with g about 11.3 against the 12 limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.14},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264220,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.48,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.19 deg gap in the front near the g-limited end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":25707,"type":"result","duration_ms":45838,"uuid":"7ea77e85-b498-4873-b849-fda2da83b2cd","ttft_stream_ms":2818,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":2818,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
